drumee-server-pod (2.9.95) stable; urgency=medium

  * Actually start the server after installing it. A from-scratch install
    finished reporting success with nothing listening: nginx up, pm2 daemon not
    even running, every page 502. Nothing brought the stack up until a reboot,
    an hour's wait for the watchdog cron, or a manual `drumee start` — the worst
    shape of failure, because the installer says Done.
    .
    Cause: dh_installinit emits its `invoke-rc.d drumee-server-pod start` BEFORE
    dh_installsystemd's block, and that block is where the unit first gets
    enabled — with no daemon-reload in between. On a genuinely fresh install
    systemd does not know the unit yet, so invoke-rc.d silently does nothing and
    returns 0. Confirmed by wiping the same box twice: the first reinstall did
    start it (systemd still had the unit cached from before the purge, journal
    shows Starting/Finished), the second, with systemd's state cleared too,
    produced no journal entry at all. Running the generated block standalone
    starts the unit fine, which is what made this look like it worked.
    .
    Second defect in the same place: drumee-ui-pod depends on this package, so
    dpkg configures the UI afterwards. Even when the start did fire, it brought
    the stack up against a UI that was not installed yet.
  * Both are fixed by taking the start away from debhelper (--no-start on
    dh_installinit and dh_installsystemd — the unit is still installed and
    enabled) and giving it to a self-interest dpkg trigger. dpkg runs triggered
    maintainer scripts once every other package in the transaction is
    configured, which is the only point at which this stack can correctly come
    up. The handler does its own daemon-reload first, uses restart so one verb
    covers fresh installs and upgrades, and is never fatal: a stack that failed
    to start is one command away from fixed, while a postinst exiting non-zero
    leaves the package half-configured and blocks every later apt run.
  * Upstream changes in this build: server-core ^1.1.81; account-purge no longer
    hands a workspace back to the account being deleted; welcome_seen drives
    Modal B post-redirect; drumate deletion is immediate rather than a freeze;
    cron dependency declared (#146).

 -- Somanos Sar <somanos.sar@drumee.com>  Sat, 01 Aug 2026 16:10:00 +0200

